       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to **7,650 mg/day**. That is three times the FDA maximum of 2,550 mg/day. A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum daily dose.\n- **2,550 mg total daily**, divided differently, such as 1,275 mg twice daily.\n- A lower dose, since many patients start at 500 mg once or twice daily and titrate up.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 2550 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly, and I'll add a note to the order saying it was intentionally confirmed."
